course: dictionary
lesson: 12778
title: Effectiveness: how well something works
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Effectiveness is how well something works, or how well it does the job it is meant to do. The adjective is effective: a good soap is effective at removing dirt.
explain: «We tested the effectiveness of three soaps by washing the same muddy hands with each one.» Effectiveness here means how well each soap got the mud off. The soap that removed the most mud has the most effectiveness.
explain: To test effectiveness fairly, change only one thing, keep everything else the same, and compare the results. Then ask: which one did its job best?
fact: Effectiveness means how well something works or does the job it is meant to do.
fact: Effective is the adjective: «The effective soap removed all the mud.»
fact: In science, effectiveness is measured by comparing results, for example how well a soap removes dirt.
fact: «The effectiveness of the magnet was tested with paper clips.»
fact: Effectiveness is uncountable, so say «the effectiveness», not «an effectiveness».
exercise: «The effectiveness of the soap was tested on muddy hands.» What does effectiveness mean here? | How much the soap smells | How well the soap cleaned the mud | How many bubbles the soap makes | *How well the soap did its job
exercise: Maya says effectiveness is just a fancy word for size. What is the better meaning? | The size of a thing | *How well something does its job | How long a test takes | The colour of a test
exercise: Which phrase means checking how well something works? | *test the effectiveness | improve effectiveness | a big effectiveness | the effectiveness bottle
test: «We compared the results to find which sun cream had the best effectiveness.» What does effectiveness mean in this sentence? | How many people bought each one | The price of each sun cream | How pretty the bottle looked | *How well each sun cream did its job
test: Which word is the adjective form of effectiveness? | effects | effectively | *effective | effectiveness
exam: «The scientist wrote down the effectiveness of each magnet by counting how many paper clips it lifted.» What did the scientist measure to find the effectiveness? | The colour of each magnet | *How well each magnet did its job | How many scientists were in the room | The weight of the box
